{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"penetration testing penetration testing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","fileName":"Penetration Testing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Penetration Testing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 00:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience]] [[Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Secure Software Development Lifecycle","Security Code Review","Security Architecture Analysis","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"penetration testing penetration testing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","fileName":"Penetration Testing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Penetration Testing","heading":"Penetration Testing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Penetration testing deliberately attempts to circumvent a system's protections and gain unauthorized logical access. It is used to find security gaps before an uncontrolled attacker exploits them.\n\nCloud services can schedule penetration tests as part of proactive monitoring and assurance, subject to the provider's rules and the system's scope. Findings should lead to remediation and retesting rather than serving only as a one-time report.\n\nPenetration testing belongs throughout a [[Secure Software Development Lifecycle]] rather than only after construction. Used alongside [[Security Code Review]] and [[Security Architecture Analysis]], it can reveal exploitable behavior early enough to change the design as well as the deployment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Secure Software Development Lifecycle","Security Code Review","Security Architecture Analysis","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"penetration testing penetration testing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Penetration Testing.md","fileName":"Penetration Testing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Penetration Testing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Secure Software Development Lifecycle","Security Code Review","Security Architecture Analysis","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}